WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.062
Let’s walk through Timeline.

00:00:02.062 --> 00:00:05.162
Use chronology to test sequence, identify gaps, and

00:00:05.162 --> 00:00:07.425
avoid duplicate interpretation.

00:00:07.425 --> 00:00:10.025
The timeline explains how the session developed;

00:00:10.025 --> 00:00:13.900
the owning artifact remains authoritative for current workflow state.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:17.400
On this slide, reconstruct when artifacts, RFIs,

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.312
messages, captures, and updates occurred.

00:00:20.312 --> 00:00:23.975
In practice, sequence explains how the session developed;

00:00:23.975 --> 00:00:27.625
the artifact surface remains the source for current workflow state

00:00:27.625 --> 00:00:27.788
.

00:00:28.285 --> 00:00:31.135
When you are ready, use Open Timeline to move

00:00:31.135 --> 00:00:32.623
to the live surface.

00:00:32.623 --> 00:00:35.335
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:35.485
.
